Package: egcar
Type: Package
Title: Accelerated Sparse Generalized Correlation Analysis via Regression
Version: 0.2.5
Authors@R: c(person("EGCAR", "Contributors", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "maintainer@example.org"),
    person("Claire", "Donnat", role = "cph",
    comment = "Bundled MIT-licensed initializer helpers"))
Description: Fits separate entrywise and view-wise row-group sparse generalized
    correlation estimators using accelerated alternating direction updates,
    cached spectral reductions, and localized loading extraction. Includes
    direct-penalty cross-validation, rate-scaled fits, reusable common folds,
    and optional common-loss comparison wrappers for sparse generalized
    correlation analysis, regularized and sparse generalized canonical
    correlation analysis, and penalized multiset canonical correlation analysis.
    Based on the accompanying research implementation. The maintainer field
    is a placeholder for local research use and must be replaced for publication.
License: GPL-3
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.0.0)
Imports: Rcpp, stats, utils
LinkingTo: Rcpp, RcppArmadillo, RcppEigen
Suggests: future, future.apply, RSpectra, RhpcBLASctl, RGCCA, PMA,
    ggplot2, remotes, testthat (>= 3.0.0), roxygen2
SystemRequirements: C++14
NeedsCompilation: yes
Config/testthat/edition: 3
